<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27662" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Māia</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Māja</span></b>  (written by Cicero <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Majja</span></b> , like ejjus,
		pejjus, etc.; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>v. the letter J),
				ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μαῖα</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Daughter of Atlas and Pleione, and the mother of
				Mercury by Jupiter</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				3, 22, 56</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Majā genitum demittit ab alto,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Mercury</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 1, 297</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Maiā natus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 6, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 11, 303</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 12, 19</span></i>;
			acc. Majam, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 4, 174</span></i>.—As <i>one of the Pleiades</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanctissima Maja,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Arat. 270</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multi ante occasum Majae coepere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 225</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 4, 174</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5,
			85</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A daughter of Faunus</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 12</span></i>.</div>
